# GUI test protocol

Input:
  <tests>: a list of test classes of Controllers/test/agentTools.
  <desks>: a list of desks.
A desk is the desk of the machine running the protocol, or a VM of that machine.
The protocol is the same on every desk: only opening and closing a desk differ.
On the Linux machine the desks are ubuntu_gnome (the desk of the machine) and the VMs of /data/gym/gui_vms_gym.txt.
<workspace> is the fearlessBranch folder of the outer agent, for example /data/fearlessBranch1.

## Agents

outer agent: the session running the protocol. It runs `protocol` and the commands it names; it never answers an action of a test.
OperatorAgent: Opus 5.5, medium effort. A new one for each test on each desk. It prepares the test, judges the run and records the values.
UserAgent: Haiku 5.5, low effort. A new one for each test on each desk. It is the person at the desk: it answers the actions of the test.
The OperatorAgent and the UserAgent know only the texts the outer agent sends them.

The outer agent must be able to start agents; an agent started by another agent cannot start agents.
An outer agent that cannot start agents runs nothing of the protocol: it tells the user it cannot start the OperatorAgent and the UserAgent, and stops.

## protocol (outer agent)

  for desk in <desks>:
    for test in <tests>:
      operator= start OperatorAgent with text(prepare)
      if reply(operator) ends with the line "passed": tell the user reply(operator); continue
      user= start UserAgent with text(answer)
      while true:
        send operator text(judge), where <report> is reply(user)
        if reply(operator) ends with the line "restart":
          run resetDesk, then startTest
          send user "The test started again."
          continue
        tell the user reply(operator)
        break

`send a t` sends the text t to the agent a and waits for its reply; reply(a) is the last reply of a.
text(t) is the text t below, where the outer agent writes out <test>, <desk>, <workspace> and <report>, and replaces each {name} with the text named name.
stopTest, startTest and resetDesk are the commands of the text commands.

## Texts

